WEBVTT

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:10.650
{=0}Green Room for
Uramichi Omota-sama

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:16.040
Uramichi-<i>san</i>!

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:20.540
Uramichi-<i>san</i>?

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:25.500
He isn't responding at all.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.010
I wonder if he's dead.

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:28.550
What?

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:34.350
U... ra... mi... chi... -<i>san</i>!

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:41.100
Whoa!

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:42.980
What the...

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:45.520
What...?

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:55.780
Come to think of it, he told me
to try not to make him turn his head

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:58.410
because he strained his neck in his sleep.

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:00.290
You should've told me sooner!

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:02.790
I bet it was on purpose, you jerk!

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:34.000
"LIFE LESSONS WITH URAMICHI ONIISAN"

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:39.800
Episode 11: Fateful Encounter

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:39.430
Hello, kids! How are you?!

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:40.350
I'm your--

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:43.140
Hey, stop! Stop!

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:44.180
Yes?

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:45.440
This isn't good!

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:48.360
It's always the same.
I've gotten tired of it.

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:52.940
Can't you come up with... more variations
of how you greet the kids?!

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:56.030
Like, you call out to them
while turning your head?

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:02.790
Hello, kids!

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:05.960
How are... Ow!

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:08.040
What's wrong, Oniisan?

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:09.040
Growing old?

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:10.250
Aging?

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:13.710
I want to deny it,
but it's pretty spot on!

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:16.930
You can't move your neck when you get old?

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:20.930
Yeah, when you get old, you can
no longer be sure what's going on

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:23.680
with all sorts of parts of your body.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:27.060
But, kids. You don't have
to be afraid of anything.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:31.690
Each of you will have
your own different future,

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:35.650
but there are certain things
that you'll all experience equally.

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:40.070
Me not being able to move
my neck right now is one of them.

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:41.910
I don't want that.

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:47.120
I didn't want it, either! But still,
I somehow became like this.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:49.000
Poor thing.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.750
Okay, kids! Let's have fun playing!

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:53.420
Yaay!

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:56.840
Oniisan. Let's play Acchi Muite Hoi!
Acchi Muite Hoi!

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:58.630
Let's not!

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:03.050
Wow, this is good!
Uramichi-<i>kun </i>is the best.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:04.060
Derekida-<i>san</i>.

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:05.140
Hm?

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:06.470
The thing is...

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:11.860
What?! What'd you say?!

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:15.070
Something is wrong with the video data
for "Traffic Safety: Right-Left Man"

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:19.360
that we shot last week,
and so we can't use it?!

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:22.820
Uramichi-<i>kun </i>taught the kids how
important it is to check right and left

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:27.080
before crossing the street by using
his entire body, mainly his neck!

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:30.750
And you're saying that
we have to re-shoot that?!

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:33.710
What do we do?! The segment
is set to start tomorrow!

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:38.420
We have to teach children the
importance of checking both ways!

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:41.930
We can't change the content now!

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:44.680
Various people did
various things for this

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:45.640
Oniisan. What's the matter?

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:48.430
because they wanted
to get various things right!

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:48.430
Do you want to play Acchi Muite Hoi?

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:50.890
We can do various things
thanks to various things!

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:54.770
Agh! Get various things ready right away!

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:56.400
Uramichi Oniisan!

00:04:58.280 --> 00:04:59.570
Listen, kids!

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:03.780
Let's have fun learning
about traffic safety today!

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:05.570
"Traffic Safety"

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:05.950
Gather around!

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:11.620
I'm going to use the crosswalk, hop!

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:14.000
Ah!

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:17.340
Usao-<i>kun</i>! Don't ignore the traffic light!

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:22.720
Hop! I'm only five years old, so I don't
know how traffic lights work, hop!

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:25.050
Jeez... What do we do with you?

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:26.390
Hop!

00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:28.100
At times like this...

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:31.520
That's right! Let's try
calling out to Right-Left Man!

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:33.100
One, two...

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:35.730
Right-Left Man!

00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:39.690
I'm right here!

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:43.950
It's sometimes important to go straight
without hesitation in your life!

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:48.950
But remember! When you make hasty actions,
it takes only one mistake

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:51.910
for you to get hurt so badly
that you can't even recover!

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:53.240
"Slow"

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:58.420
So, when you make important choices,
make sure you check right and left!

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:58.500
"Traffic Safety"      "Crossing"

